content.text:
I found an important distinction:

Spawning a dire wolf does not activate its aura. It only gives the wolf the `wolf_howl` ability. The howl itself is gated by:

- line of sight;
- 60% chance;
- one-turn telegraph;
- 10-turn cooldown.

The aura should appear only after the howl actually fires. You should see the combat message:

> “The dire wolf throws back its head and howls…”

The rules → WorldView → self-glow path is now regression-tested and passes. I committed that coverage as `c0dbf20cb`.

If you are seeing the howl message but still no green glow on the wolf or rats, then the remaining bug is specifically in the live display/runtime path.

